description:
Closes rstudio/packrat#559 by following pattern from rstudio/packrat#481. 

@kevinushey -- let me know if you have any suggestions/edits. I've tested locally and on deploy to RStudio Connect (after replacing tarball of `packrat` on Connect server) with following in RMarkdown:
```{r}
devtools::install_gitlab("alexkgold/riskgauge_pub")
riskgauge::add2(1, 1)
```

Related to #490 

This adds a failing test to aid in test-driven-development and to illustrate the behavior that is going awry on RStudio Connect.

@aronatkins @kevinushey FYI.  I can provide the support ticket link if it is helpful.

This fix should allow multiple R sessions of the same version to use the same packrat `lib-R` directory.

This is done by ensuring pre-existing symlinks are only updated in a new version of R is detected (ie, with the session R not equal to the version of R associated with `base` in `lib-R`).

@jjallaire, can you double check that this is sensible? I think it should ensure any pre-existing packrat + RStudio machinery should play nicely together.
